      "type": "text",
      "text": "{\"unit_id\": \"Minemaes\", \"choices\": [\"C1\"], \"reasoning\": \"C1 Mnw-ms.w (Min-mesu) is made of the god Min plus ms.w 'born of'. Minemaes reads as Min + e + maes, with consonants m-n-m-s. Every consonant matches, the final w is a weak consonant that can go unwritten, and the vowels are added by convention. So it is the same name. C2 Jmn-ms.w (Amun-mesu) is made of the god Amun plus ms.w. Its consonants j-m-n-m-s could in principle match m-n-m-s if the weak j is dropped. But 'Mine-' renders the god Min, not Amun, which would be written Amen- or Amun-. Record 1 therefore reads as different words, and C2 is a different name.\"}"
